The round-two repairs for cross-object comparisons, evidence destinations, two blind holdout readers, H4’s stated period conflict, and preserving H2’s later deadline are present in the revised plan. H3 now names its conflicting separation rule; H6 and H7 clearly present their leans as choices.

I reran the census read-only and verified the reported **69/122/39/2** and **17/32/12/1** question/candidate/merge/succession counts, plus the four displayed evidence counts. I also checked the earlier gold’s individual labels: **23 keep, 12 duplicate, 10 do not open, five borderline**. The verdict categories remain provisional because the script parses reason text. I did not independently verify every quotation, archived classification, estimate, or factual claim in the plan.

