53:    53	## Ladder
76:    76	5. Numeric theses name a year. Non-company quantities use calendar years: the publication year is this year and the following year is next year, each ending December 31. Company quantities use the fiscal year containing publication day and its successor. Never use the computer clock. For a given quantity, open at most one thesis for each of this year and next year; do not open later years. The due date is the quantity's publication date.
126:   126	- Dependencies and the theme block are the two ways theses influence each other; succession only orders periods. B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion. The theme block (D191, D195) shows every open, judged theme thesis to every asset thesis's judgement, one to all, and the judgement states which way each theme it weighed pushes it; no edge is written for it. Keep B's direct evidence separate from dependency states and reasons. A's conclusion can affect B like evidence but is not stored as evidence: external events and statements are evidence, whereas A is our own judgement. Treating it as evidence would let the system convince itself.
133:   133	## Succession: the same focus over successive periods
136:   136	- Successive periods of the same focus form a chain, such as Fed year-end 2026 rate → 2027 rate → 2028 rate. The chain records period order. Dependency traversal follows the rules above.
148:   148	| Chain | Succession: Fed year-end 2026 rate → 2027 → 2028 | Replacement: AMZN capex guidance 12% growth → 25% |
163:   163	  ↓ 4 Match (Model): The model does not read the original item. Show each existing thesis's subject, question, focus, ladder, due date and open/closed state. In one call: (1) decide candidate identity or a narrower part, succession with unchanged ladder orientation but new thresholds, new thesis for distinct or merely similar questions, or skip overly broad questions, numbers beyond this/next year and the same period of a closed thesis; give reasons; (2) choose dependencies and directions among searched, block-5 and same-item new theses; (3) compare evidence linked only to existing theses. Evidence linked to candidates waits for their destinations, then searches all linked existing theses together and uses one further comparison call. Evidence linked only to new theses is new evidence.
176:   176	| Succession | The next period of the same focus: the next year for numbers, or continued tracking after an event thesis closed | Create a thesis and record succession |
