docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/review-drift-v2.12.md:7:   - **Gold entries for rejected statements have no valid label in some cases.** [§8.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/standard-v2.12.md:297) requires every sentence that looks like evidence but is rejected to be assigned to a row in §5.3: “看起来像证据但不留的句子各属于 §5.3 哪一行.” Yet [§5.3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/standard-v2.12.md:197) says sentences outside that list must be judged under §5.1. An unrelated claim can therefore be rejected under the relevance rule without belonging to any §5.3 row. The signed standard does not impose this labelling requirement, and it is in neither top list.
